// std/element.bpa — the shared element carrier.
//
// A single abstract sort of "elements", imported by the theories that range
// over a common domain (sets, relations) so they COMPOSE: a relation's elements
// are exactly a set's elements, one underlying sort. Sort aliasing
// (`sort Universe = element.Element`) is real identification — the local name
// points at this same sort — so a predicate declared over `Element` here accepts
// elements from any theory that shares it, and that theory's theorems apply.
//
// This is deliberately minimal: no operations, no axioms — just the carrier.

sort Element
